        "meta_description": "Starter page",
        "canonical_url": null,
        "robots": "index, follow",
        "schema_type": "WebPage",
        "og_title": null,
        "og_description": null,
        "og_image": null
      },
      "nodes": [
        {
          "node_type": "section",
          "id": "section-1",
          "section_title": null,
          "section_class": "-full-lg",
          "item_box_class": "l-box",
          "sal": "no-animation",
          "columns": [
            {
              "id": "section-1-column-1",
              "width_class": "dd-u-1-1",
              "components": [
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "# Project Outline\n## Fonts Used\nThe framework uses the Lato font family from the assets/fonts folder in the following weights:\n\n- 300 (Light)\n- 400 (Regular)\n- 700 (Bold)\n\nCSS file location to update fonts: `source/scss/partials/_fonts.scss`\n\n## Colors Used\nThe framework defines a comprehensive color system including:\n\n- Primary colors (brand identity)\n- Action colors (CTAs, buttons, interactions)\n- Semantic colors (success, warning, error, info)\n- Text role colors\n- Neutral UI colors\n- Support/utility colors\n- Admin button colors\n- Social media colors\n\nCSS file location to update colors: `source/scss/partials/_variables.scss`\n\n## Source SCSS Folder Structure\n- dd-framework.scss: Main framework entry point\n- style.scss: Primary stylesheet entry point\n- vendors/: Styles for third-party libraries (e.g., SAL)\n- components/: SCSS files for reusable UI components (e.g., accordions, banners, cards)\n- drupal-components/: Styles specific to Drupal CMS components\n- elements/: Base styles for HTML elements (forms, tables, text, etc.)\n- fonts/: Local fonts\n- layouts/: Page-specific layout styles\n- partials/: Utility files including variables, mixins, fonts, grid system, and custom animations\n- regions/: Styles for page regions (header, footer, sidebar)\n\n## Source JS Folder Structure\n- main.js: Main JavaScript entry point\n- components/: JavaScript files for interactive components (e.g., navigation, sliders, tabs)\n- vendors/: Third-party JavaScript libraries (e.g., SAL)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "export_dir": "web",
  "base_url": "https://framework.ldnddev.com/",
  "lang": "en",
  "pretty_urls": true
}